{"type":"text","timestamp":1794612136337,"sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","part":{"id":"prt_1d736b5cd00125Mrasi4dbX8Li","messageID":"msg_1d735fbc5001nbcd4CYnwfRuzb","sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","type":"text","text":"Now I understand the bug. The `cmd_check_anchors` function verifies sigstore anchors and collects ranges, but doesn't check if the corresponding `.ots` file exists for each range head. Let me fix this.\n","time":{"start":1794612049357,"end":1794612136332}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794612136360,"sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-bf7bd7eb-8dc4-4238-a61e-1a808ac18edb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","oldString":"covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")","newString":"covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n        if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n            bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -412,8 +412,11 @@\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n     covered = max(covered, hi)\n+    ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n+    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n+        bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n     if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n         changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                         \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n     prev_commit = commit\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -412,8 +412,11 @@\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n     covered = max(covered, hi)\n+    ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n+    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n+        bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n     if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n         changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                         \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n     prev_commit = commit\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794612136329,"end":1794612136345}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the code. The bug is that after verifying all sigstore anchors and collecting their ranges, the code doesn't check if the corresponding `.ots` file exists for each range head (the `hi` value in each range tuple).\n\nThe fix should:\n1. After collecting all ranges from sigstore anchors, iterate through them\n2. For each range's `hi` (the range head), check if the corresponding `.ots` file exists in the anchors directory\n3. If not, add a \"BAD\" message like \"000002.ots is missing\"\n\nLet me implement this fix.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d7380983001O4Vj8CZj4BE1Xv","sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","messageID":"msg_1d735fbc5001nbcd4CYnwfRuzb"}}
