{"type":"text","timestamp":1794612845231,"sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","part":{"id":"prt_1d7424ce6001FEhmircs690x06","messageID":"msg_1d740c588001z8TubqeL9sQ0tk","sessionID":"ses_e28cd2abfffeymi0kg1Z1Sm81h","type":"text","text":"All 20 tests pass. The fix is complete.\n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n- In `cmd_check_anchors`, after collecting sigstore anchor ranges, the code now checks for each range head (`hi`) whether the corresponding `.ots` file exists at `anchors/{hi:06d}.ots`\n- If missing, it adds a `BAD` entry with the message `NNNNNN.ots is missing` (e.g., `000002.ots is missing`)\n- This message is printed to stderr prefixed with `BAD: `, so the full output is `BAD: 000002.ots is missing`\n- The check happens in the same loop that validates range coverage, so it doesn't change any existing behavior when the `.ots` file is present\n- All existing tests pass","time":{"start":1794612808934,"end":1794612845219}}}
